From 804a18f9b5338765171b77b60710b1f588c3f851 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linyao01 <linyao01@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:01:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(pay): sign under a per-call EIP-712 domain, not the
 global one

boat_nano_sign, the x402 client and attestation's x402 path each set the
global domain separator and then signed with it. On a device where the
nanopayment buyer, anchoring and x402 run on different tasks, one task
could sign under another's domain. tests/test_domain_race.c, two threads
signing under a Gateway and a token domain, got 1 of 800 signatures
wrong in each of three runs before this change and 0 after it.

- boat_pay_authorize_ext(kp, params, chain_id, contract, name, version,
  sig): computes the domain separator per call, touches no global
- boat_nano_sign, the x402 V2 client and attestation's x402 V2 path use
  it, and no longer set the global domain
- boat_pay_authorize copies the global domain before using it; it stays
  for callers that set the domain themselves (x402 V1)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
